1.What are directives, custom directives with explanation 
  Directives in Angular are classes that extend the behavior of DOM elements.
  Angular mainly has two types of directives:  
  1. Structural Directives
  These modify the DOM structure by adding or removing elements.
  Examples include *ngIf, *ngFor, and *ngSwitch.  
  2. Attribute Directives
  These change the appearance or behavior of existing elements without changing the DOM structure.
  Examples include ngClass, ngStyle, and custom attribute directives.  
  Components are a special type of directive that include a template and styles, and Angular applications
  are primarily component-based.  
  Angular also allows creating custom structural and attribute directives to encapsulate reusable DOM behavior.

  @Input and @Output are used for component communication, not directives.Directives in 
